-- India worked example, second round: Kerala, and language and schooling policy. All of it is AI-drafted and unreviewed by an Indian curriculum expert.
--
-- 1. A new Kerala School Curriculum Repository, nested under the India repository. The existing Kerala repository holds separate research on
--    the education of Scheduled Tribe communities that has not been reviewed, so it is not linked here: a link gives a space's members
--    read access to every record in the repository it points at.
-- 2. 52 records (34 kerala, 10 india, 3 karnataka, 3 maharashtra, 2 uttar-pradesh), each with the document it was read from and the passage. Summaries are in our own words.
-- 3. Each synthetic space is declared as grounded in the Kerala repository, so its members can read it.
-- 4. 20 proposed links from parts of the spaces to those records. Their relation type starts with proposed_, which the views show as
--    "AI-drafted, unconfirmed". A person confirms, edits or removes each one.
-- 5. 1 correction to earlier records.
-- Needs migration 200 (the India repositories and views) applied first; it stops with an error otherwise, so nothing is skipped without notice.
--
-- To undo, delete exactly these records (their links go with them), then the Kerala repository link rows and the Kerala repository:
